Nokia 6 (PLE) vendor preparation for LineageOS 23.2
================================================

Place the three repositories at device/nokia/PLE, vendor/nokia/PLE and
kernel/nokia/msm8937 in the Android source checkout. No Nokia common tree
is used. Keep all proprietary outputs private: redistribution is not qualified.
The ignored proprietary/ directory is intentionally absent after Git clone.

Requirements
------------

Linux, Python 3.11+, Bash, Git, readelf (binutils), and the Android checkout's
prebuilts/extract-tools/linux-x86/bin/patchelf-0_17_2 and patchelf-0_18.
The selected clang-r563880c prebuilt supplies llvm-strip for the accepted netmgr
ELF metadata normalization; final full-file digests verify the result.
No SDK jar, Gradle cache or out/ build artifact is used to prepare the payload.

Inputs
------

1. An already-extracted exact Nokia Android 9 00WW_6_19F filesystem root,
   containing system/. Every selected stock file is verified against its
   recorded SHA256. The script does not extract ZIPs, access a phone or flash.

2. The existing, narrowly selected Mi8937 GPU PFP compatibility input:
   https://github.com/TheMuppets/proprietary_vendor_xiaomi_Mi8937
   Recorded source revision: aae77327cb51edcfdbaa7df1e2e08fae19784f36
   File: proprietary/vendor/firmware/a530_pfp.fw
   SHA256: 072cbbb67eeb67689fd3ba2c11708e0778ae873b42d79cac030821e12fbcd126
   Pass its repository/extracted source root. Only this exact file is consumed;
   neither another firmware set nor a stock PFP with different bytes is accepted.
   The content hash is authoritative even if that root has a different HEAD.

Prepare a fresh private payload
------------------------------

From the Android source root, with the actual input directories substituted:

  ./vendor/nokia/PLE/extract-files.sh \
      --stock-root /absolute/path/to/extracted-619F-root \
      --gpu-pfp-reference-root /absolute/path/to/pinned-Mi8937-vendor-root

The default destination is vendor/nokia/PLE/proprietary. When running outside
the Android checkout or preparing a comparison copy, supply:

  --android-root /absolute/path/to/lineage-23.2 \
  --output /absolute/path/to/new-proprietary-directory

The output's parent directory must exist. Existing files/directories/symlinks
are refused, including a concurrently created destination. There is no --force.
Preserve an existing working payload separately before any manual replacement.

Preparation validates every stock input, uses isolated component directories,
retains the existing guarded camera/audio/Goodix/radio/sensor fixups, merges the
explicit mappings and verifies all 401 output SHA256 values and file modes in
config/payload-digests.tsv. Only then is the new directory published atomically.
This includes both exact PLE Wi-Fi inputs and the non-BAM radio variant.
Historical unused audio-msm8937 archive copies are not needed or regenerated.
No current Make/Blueprint selection is regenerated or overwritten.

Relevant records
----------------

config/blob-spec.tsv: core GPU/TEE/Vulkan inputs and source authorities.
config/manifests/: stock hashes; wifi.tsv records the two exact Wi-Fi paths.
config/payload-groups.json: explicit component-to-final-path mapping.
config/payload-digests.tsv: accepted final content hashes and modes.
config/provenance/: retained component extraction/fixup provenance.
tools/: component extractors used by the complete preparation entry point.

Apply platform patches and build
--------------------------------

  ./device/nokia/PLE/patches/apply.sh --source . --check
  ./device/nokia/PLE/patches/apply.sh --source .

Follow device/nokia/PLE/patches/README.md for the ordered platform series and
optional --strict-base reproduction mode. A compatible upstream commit does
not relax the exact stock/PFP payload hashes or hardware ABI constraints.

Use the normal LineageOS build environment and select lineage_PLE-userdebug.
These instructions do not claim a full clean-build or hardware qualification
for arbitrary newer upstream revisions. Never flash a build without checking
its target, recovery path and the device's current partition arrangement.
